  },
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash|PowerShell|Monitor",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "powershell.exe",
            "args": [
              "-NoProfile",
              "-ExecutionPolicy",
              "Bypass",
              "-Command",
              "try { & '${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}\\hooks\\PreToolUse-Guard.ps1'; exit $LASTEXITCODE } catch { [Console]::Error.WriteLine('PreToolUse guard could not run - blocking: ' + $_); exit 2 }"
            ],
            "timeout": 60
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "env": {
    "DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER": "1",
    "DISABLE_ERROR_REPORTING": "1",
    "CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_AUTO_MEMORY": "1",
    "BASH_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS": "1800000",
    "BASH_MAX_TIMEOUT_MS": "5400000"
  },
  "autoUpdatesChannel": "stable",
  "_hooks_comment": "Exec form (command + args): Claude Code substitutes ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR} as a plain string and runs powershell.exe directly, so no shell (Git Bash vs PowerShell) ever re-parses this line. The -Command wrapper makes a MISSING or crashing guard script exit 2 (blocking) instead of exit 1 (which the harness treats as non-blocking, i.e. fail-open). Hooks in a project settings file run in a `claude -p` session even when the folder was never trusted (docs: permissions#what-runs-before-you-trust-a-folder). Start-Repair.ps1 additionally proves the guard blocks on this machine before every run (hook canary). Limitation: a kit path containing a single quote breaks the wrapper - keep the drive path plain.",
  "_deny_comment": "Enforced in every permission mode. Scope: verbs that are never part of a repair, plus deletion of a protected ROOT (C:\\, C:\\Windows, C:\\Program Files, HKLM hives) spelled as the root followed by the next parameter or a closing quote - a subpath such as C:\\Windows\\System32\\spool\\PRINTERS\\* or a malware Run value under HKLM must stay deletable, so the old substring rules (*Remove-Item*C:\\Windows*, *Remove-Item*HKLM:\\*) were dropped; they also matched Remove-ItemProperty. Spellings a glob cannot express (path last with no trailing parameter, quoted payload inside cmd /c, aliases the harness does not canonicalize, HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE, -EncodedCommand) are caught by hooks\\PreToolUse-Guard.ps1, which re-checks the same verbs on a normalized copy of the command. Edit/Write rules use the harness's POSIX form (//c/...): a bare C:\\ pattern is treated as cwd-relative and never matches. Monitor is denied outright: it runs shell commands in the background, which the playbook forbids (a one-shot session cannot wait for them) and which the guard matcher would otherwise have to cover separately. scripts/test-deny-rules.py and scripts/test-pretooluse-guard.ps1 pin both layers.",
  "autoMemoryEnabled": false,
  "_env_comment": "BASH_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS / BASH_MAX_TIMEOUT_MS: sfc, DISM /RestoreHealth, a full msert scan and chkdsk routinely exceed the shell tool's default 10-minute cap, after which the harness backgrounds the command and the one-shot session ends without its result; 30 min default / 90 min max keep them in the foreground. Auto-memory is off: memory written under CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR (on the USB) would otherwise carry one machine's notes into the next machine's session."
}
